---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleSchema from '../../components/ArticleSchema.astro';
import FaqSection from '../../components/FaqSection.astro';
import { site } from '../../content';
const path = '/compare/yotpo-email-sms-vs-activecampaign';
const title = 'Yotpo Email & SMS to ActiveCampaign for Shopify: Migration Decision';
const desc = "Moving from retired Yotpo Email & SMS to ActiveCampaign: Shopify data, wholesale handoffs, review ownership and migration checks.";

const faqs = [
  {
    "question": "Can I choose Yotpo Email & SMS for a new store?",
    "answer": "No. Yotpo announced full deprecation for December 31, 2025; its current SMS notice says dashboard access and background services have ended."
  },
  {
    "question": "Does connecting Shopify restore my old Yotpo automations?",
    "answer": "No. A Shopify connection and a retained Yotpo export are different data sources. Rebuild entry rules, exclusions and templates from records you actually have."
  },
  {
    "question": "Will wholesale draft orders appear in ActiveCampaign?",
    "answer": "The documented Shopify sync excludes draft orders. Treat quote and draft-order workflows as a separate mapping problem rather than assuming order automation covers them."
  },
  {
    "question": "Can I keep Yotpo Reviews?",
    "answer": "Separate review collection from the replacement sender. Record which service owns each request and prove any review-status data path before using it to branch email."
  },
  {
    "question": "How should I compare cost?",
    "answer": "Request a quote for the contacts, history access, automation and sales features you need. Include retained review services, an SMS destination if required and ongoing integration work."
  },
  {
    "question": "Should Sequenzy be on the shortlist?",
    "answer": "It can be another candidate, but compare the actual Shopify events, audience controls and sales handoff requirements. No price or workflow advantage is established by this page."
  }
];
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={desc} site={site} path={path}>
  <ArticleSchema title={title} description={desc} siteName={site.name} domain={site.domain} path={path} />

  <section class="py-14 md:py-20">
    <div class="container">
      <nav class="mb-8 text-sm">
        <a class="link" href="/compare">Comparisons</a>
        <span class="mx-2 text-cyan-100/90">/</span>
        <span class="text-cyan-100/90">Yotpo Email & SMS vs ActiveCampaign</span>
      </nav>

      <header class="max-w-4xl">
        <p class="badge">Head-to-head</p>
        <h1 class="hero-title mt-5">Yotpo Email & SMS vs ActiveCampaign for Shopify</h1>
        <p class="mt-7 max-w-3xl text-xl leading-9 text-cyan-100">Yotpo Email & SMS is retired. For a Shopify merchant considering ActiveCampaign, the useful decision is how to rebuild customer messaging and sales handoffs while keeping review collection and loyalty responsibilities explicit. This guide proposes checks; it reports no merchant trial or measured result.</p>
      </header>

      <article class="prose-shopify mt-14 max-w-4xl">
        <h2>The former suite is not a current sender choice</h2>
        <p>Yotpo scheduled Email and SMS deprecation for December 31, 2025. Its current SMS notice confirms decommissioning and unavailable dashboard/background services. Do not plan a new flow in that dashboard. Start from retained exports, screenshots and support-confirmed recovery options; the old suite price is not a live alternative quote.</p>
        <h2>Start with the wholesale exception</h2>
        <p>For a hypothetical equipment shop selling both consumer products and quoted commercial orders, define what should happen when a buyer requests a quote rather than completing checkout. ActiveCampaign documents that draft orders are not synced. A purchase-triggered sequence therefore cannot be assumed to see the wholesale sales cycle. Record the source of quote status, the person responsible for the account and the event that should end follow-up.</p>
        <h2>Map contact identity before sales handoffs</h2>
        <p>Use a proposed acceptance worksheet with customer email, company, storefront tags, order identity and the sales owner. Inspect a consumer contact and a commercial buyer separately. Decide whether a person changing company or sharing a purchasing address should update an existing record or require manual review. A Shopify connection alone does not establish a full company hierarchy or a maintained sales pipeline.</p>
        <h2>Proposed test: consumer welcome versus commercial inquiry</h2>
        <p>Create controlled profiles for a retail signup, a wholesale inquiry and an existing customer who does not accept marketing. Preview the branch and recipient status before enabling any send. The commercial path should reach the designated sales owner without issuing a consumer signup discount. Record the field and source behind each exclusion, rather than relying on the name of an imported list.</p>
        <h2>Proposed test: cart, purchase and quote follow-up</h2>
        <p>Use a fresh controlled cart and then a completed purchase to inspect entry and exit behavior. Separately exercise a draft quote through its real source system. Confirm that the commercial follow-up stops when the quote closes, while a consumer purchase exits recovery. Assign responsibility for stale tasks and duplicate notifications. These are proposed checks, not claims of conversion lift or a tested native quote integration.</p>
        <h2>History is not a replay queue</h2>
        <p>ActiveCampaign documents a Shopify history sync with plan restrictions, and says historical purchases do not trigger the Makes a purchase automation. Confirm the selected plan and inspect imported records before reconstructing lapsed-buyer audiences. Do not expect old abandoned carts to restart recovery. Retain a mapping of old segment definitions to available destination data, with missing history recorded explicitly.</p>
        <h2>Keep reviews and loyalty responsibilities visible</h2>
        <p>For every post-purchase touch, list the sender, triggering event and exclusions: care instructions, review request, loyalty notification and sales follow-up. Retaining Yotpo Reviews does not restore the retired email product. If a flow depends on review completion or loyalty status, establish a supported data bridge and its maintainer; otherwise use copy that does not depend on unavailable state.</p>
        <h2>Budget for the workflow you will operate</h2>
        <p>Request a current quote with contact counts, required history access, automation features and any sales tooling specified. Add the review service, SMS service if needed and time spent repairing field mappings. Choose ActiveCampaign only if the demonstrated data and handoff workflow justify that ownership. For a simple retail program, include other candidates such as Sequenzy without assuming they solve the quote problem.</p>
        <h2>Cut over by responsibility</h2>
        <p>Recover channel-specific subscriptions and suppression records from legitimate retained sources. Keep marketing eligibility separate from the existence of a customer record. Inventory surviving Shopify and third-party recovery messages, then assign one owner per message purpose. Keep unverified imports out of active audiences and preserve the mapping and test notes for the next operator.</p>
        <h2>Sources and limits</h2>
        <p>Supplier documentation checked November 24, 2026. These are documented scope and proposed acceptance checks, not firsthand product tests. Account access, current quotes and live integration payloads remain unverified.</p>
        <ul>
          <li><a class="link" href="https://email-and-sms.yotpo.com/">Yotpo end-of-life notice</a></li>
          <li><a class="link" href="https://www.yotpo.com/blog/email-sms-migration-partners/">Yotpo sunset announcement</a></li>
          <li><a class="link" href="https://help.activecampaign.com/hc/en-us/articles/360012461899-Data-synced-from-the-ActiveCampaign-Shopify-integration">ActiveCampaign Shopify data</a></li>
          <li><a class="link" href="https://help.activecampaign.com/hc/en-us/articles/115000202150-Connect-your-Shopify-store-to-ActiveCampaign">ActiveCampaign connection and history behavior</a></li>
        </ul>
      </article>
      <div class="mt-10 max-w-4xl text-sm">
        <p class="font-black text-white">Related comparisons</p>
        <p class="mt-2">
          <a class="link" href="/compare/drip-vs-activecampaign">Drip vs ActiveCampaign</a> ·
          <a class="link" href="/compare/privy-vs-activecampaign">Privy vs ActiveCampaign</a> ·
          <a class="link" href="/compare/yotpo-email-sms-vs-drip">Yotpo vs Drip</a> ·
          <a class="link" href="/for/b2b-wholesale">Email apps for B2B wholesale</a> ·
          <a class="link" href="/for/beauty">Email apps for beauty stores</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <FaqSection faqs={faqs} title="Yotpo Email & SMS vs ActiveCampaign FAQ" />
</BaseLayout>
